//! Protobuf structures of the waywallen daemon control protocol.
//!
//! Port of `rexon/qt_wallpaper_engine/proto/control_pb2.py` + `filter_pb2.py`:
//! the code is NOT hand-written but generated by `prost-build` (build.rs) from
//! the original `control.proto`/`filter.proto`. The proto package is
//! `waywallen.control.v1`, so prost puts everything into a file with that name.
//!
//! Serialization/deserialization goes through the `prost::Message` trait
//! (`encode_to_vec` / `decode`). Parity with Python is checked by the golden
//! test `proto_parity.rs`: reference bytes were captured from `google.protobuf`
//! (`SerializeToString(deterministic=True)`), Rust decodes them and encodes them
//! again — for messages without a `map` the bytes must match exactly (both
//! proto3 implementations write fields in ascending field-number order and omit
//! defaults). `map` fields are not byte-deterministic (key order in a HashMap is
//! arbitrary), so for them the check is structural only.
//!
//! We re-export the generated module as `control` — a short path
//! `rexon_core::proto::control::Request` and so on.
pub mod control {
    include!(concat!(env!("OUT_DIR"), "/waywallen.control.v1.rs"));
}
